# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets response headers.
#
# /data/* is NOT content-addressed: the path is stable (`LT01T01.json`), so a
# redeploy replaces the bytes behind an unchanged URL. `immutable` therefore
# pins a returning visitor to whatever payload they first downloaded — a
# regenerated recording's offsets never reach them. Revalidate instead; the
# ETag makes the common case a 304.
#
# /_nuxt/* IS content-addressed (Vite hashes the filename), so immutable is
# correct there.
#
# HTML is deliberately NOT listed: Workers Static Assets already serves it with
# `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which is what a deploy
# that can change any page needs. (A `/*.html` rule would also be invalid —
# Cloudflare only supports a splat at the end of a path.)
#
# planning/performance-and-content-refactor.md §3 phase 1.

/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/_nuxt/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
